  "worked_solution": "The integral is defined over a type II region.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{1}^{{y}^{3}}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}[{\\int }_{1}^{{y}^{3}}dx]\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}[x]_{1}^{{y}^{3}}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}({y}^{3}-1)\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}(y-\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}})\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{4}(y-\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}})\\,dy & ={[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{1}{y}]}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =(8+\\frac{1}{4})-(\\frac{1}{2}+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{27}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
